{"id":"mahabharata-9-035","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":35,"title":"पञ्चत्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 35 · The tirthas of Trita and Udapana","summary":{"en":"Balarama visits the well-tirtha of the sage Trita, and the story is told of how Trita, thrown into a well by his brothers, performed a sacrifice from within it. The gods came and Trita cursed his brothers to become wolves.","kn":"ಬಲರಾಮ ತ್ರಿತ ಋಷಿಯ ಬಾವಿ ತೀರ್ಥಕ್ಕೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಸಹೋದರರು ಬಾವಿಗೆ ಎಸೆದ ತ್ರಿತ ಅದರೊಳಗಿಂದಲೇ ಯಜ್ಞ ಮಾಡಿದ ಕಥೆ ಹೇಳಲ್ಪಡುತ್ತದೆ. ದೇವತೆಗಳು ಬಂದರು; ತ್ರಿತ ತನ್ನ ಸಹೋದರರು ತೋಳಗಳಾಗಲೆಂದು ಶಪಿಸಿದನು.","hi":"बलराम ऋषि त्रित के कूप-तीर्थ पर जाते हैं, और कथा कही जाती है कि भाइयों द्वारा कुएँ में फेंके गए त्रित ने उसी के भीतर से यज्ञ किया। देवता आए और त्रित ने भाइयों को भेड़िये बनने का शाप दिया।","te":"బలరాముడు త్రిత ఋషి బావి తీర్థానికి వెళతాడు; సోదరులు బావిలో పడవేసిన త్రితుడు దాని లోపల నుండే యజ్ఞం చేసిన కథ చెప్పబడుతుంది. దేవతలు వచ్చారు; త్రితుడు సోదరులను తోడేళ్లు కమ్మని శపించాడు.","ta":"பலராமன் முனிவர் த்ரிதரின் கிணற்றுத் தீர்த்தத்துக்குச் செல்ல, சகோதரர்களால் கிணற்றில் தள்ளப்பட்ட த்ரிதர் அதனுள்ளிருந்தே வேள்வி செய்த கதை கூறப்படுகிறது. தேவர் வர, த்ரிதர் தம் சகோதரர் ஓநாய்களாகட்டும் என்று சபித்தார்.","ml":"ബലരാമൻ ത്രിതൻ എന്ന ഋഷിയുടെ കിണർ-തീർത്ഥം സന്ദർശിക്കുന്നു; സഹോദരന്മാർ ഒരു കിണറ്റിൽ തള്ളിയിട്ട ത്രിതൻ, അതിനുള്ളിൽനിന്ന് യജ്ഞം ചെയ്ത കഥ പറയുന്നു. ദേവന്മാർ വന്നപ്പോൾ, ത്രിതൻ സഹോദരന്മാരെ ചെന്നായ്ക്കളാകട്ടെ എന്ന് ശപിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.35; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"सारस्वतपर्व","titleEn":"Sarasvata Parva (Balarama's pilgrimage on the Sarasvati)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तस्मान्नदीगतं चापि उदपानं यशस्विनः ।\nत्रितस्य च महाराज जगामाथ हलायुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the renowned Halayudha, Balarama, went on to the well of Trita on the river's bank, great king."}},{"n":2,"text":"तत्र दत्त्वा बहु द्रव्यं पूजयित्वा तथा द्विजान् ।\nउपस्पृश्य च तत्रैव प्रहृष्टो मुसलायुधः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he gave away much wealth, honored the Brahmins, performed the ritual touching of water, and the wielder of the club-plough was delighted."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र धर्मपरो ह्यासीत्त्रितः स सुमहातपाः ।\nकूपे च वसता तेन सोमः पीतो महात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita, of great austerity, had been devoted to dharma there, and while living in that well that great soul had drunk soma."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्र चैनं समुत्सृज्य भ्रातरौ जग्मतुर्गृहान् ।\nततस्तौ वै शशापाथ त्रितो ब्राह्मणसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His two brothers left him there and went home, and then Trita, best of Brahmins, cursed them."}},{"text":"जनमेजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Janamejaya said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"उदपानं कथं ब्रह्मन्कथं च सुमहातपाः ।\nपतितः किं च संत्यक्तो भ्रातृभ्यां द्विजसत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, how did that well come to be, and how did that man of great austerity, best of the twice-born, fall in and get abandoned by his brothers?"}},{"n":6,"text":"कूपे कथं च हित्वैनं भ्रातरौ जग्मतुर्गृहान् ।\nएतदाचक्ष्व मे ब्रह्मन्यदि श्राव्यं हि मन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"How did his brothers leave him in the well and go home? Tell me this, Brahmin, if you think it fit to be heard."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"आसन्पूर्वयुगे राजन्मुनयो भ्रातरस्त्रयः ।\nएकतश्च द्वितश्चैव त्रितश्चादित्यसंनिभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, in an earlier age there were three brother sages: Ekata, Dvita and Trita, radiant as the sun."}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्वे प्रजापतिसमाः प्रजावन्तस्तथैव च ।\nब्रह्मलोकजितः सर्वे तपसा ब्रह्मवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All were equal to the Prajapatis, had children, had won the world of Brahma by austerity, and were speakers of the Veda."}},{"n":9,"text":"तेषां तु तपसा प्रीतो नियमेन दमेन च ।\nअभवद्गौतमो नित्यं पिता धर्मरतः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gautama, ever devoted to dharma, was pleased by their austerity, discipline and self-control, and became their constant father."}},{"n":10,"text":"स तु दीर्घेण कालेन तेषां प्रीतिमवाप्य च ।\nजगाम भगवान्स्थानमनुरूपमिवात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After a long time, having gained their affection, the blessed Gautama departed to a place fitting for himself."}},{"n":11,"text":"राजानस्तस्य ये पूर्वे याज्या ह्यासन्महात्मनः ।\nते सर्वे स्वर्गते तस्मिंस्तस्य पुत्रानपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings who had earlier been that great soul's patrons, once he had gone to heaven, honored his sons."}},{"n":12,"text":"तेषां तु कर्मणा राजंस्तथैवाध्ययनेन च ।\nत्रितः स श्रेष्ठतां प्राप यथैवास्य पिता तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, by his rites and his study Trita rose to excellence, just as his father had."}},{"n":13,"text":"तं स्म सर्वे महाभागा मुनयः पुण्यलक्षणाः ।\nअपूजयन्महाभागं तथा विद्वत्तयैव तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the fortunate sages of auspicious marks honored the illustrious Trita for his learning as well."}},{"n":14,"text":"कदाचिद्धि ततो राजन्भ्रातरावेकतद्वितौ ।\nयज्ञार्थं चक्रतुश्चित्तं धनार्थं च विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once, king, the brothers Ekata and Dvita set their minds on a sacrifice, and especially on wealth."}},{"n":15,"text":"तयोश्चिन्ता समभवत्त्रितं गृह्य परंतप ।\nयाज्यान्सर्वानुपादाय प्रतिगृह्य पशूंस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking Trita with them, scorcher of foes, they planned to collect from all their patrons, receive animals as gifts,"}},{"n":16,"text":"सोमं पास्यामहे हृष्टाः प्राप्य यज्ञं महाफलम् ।\nचक्रुश्चैव महाराज भ्रातरस्त्रय एव ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"and happily drink soma after obtaining a sacrifice of great reward. And so the three brothers did, great king."}},{"n":17,"text":"तथा तु ते परिक्रम्य याज्यान्सर्वान्पशून्प्रति ।\nयाजयित्वा ततो याज्याँल्लब्ध्वा च सुबहून्पशून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They went about to all their patrons for animals, performed sacrifices for them, and gained very many animals."}},{"n":18,"text":"याज्येन कर्मणा तेन प्रतिगृह्य विधानतः ।\nप्राचीं दिशं महात्मान आजग्मुस्ते महर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received these by lawful rites for their priestly service, those great seers came toward the eastern quarter."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्रितस्तेषां महाराज पुरस्ताद्याति हृष्टवत् ।\nएकतश्च द्वितश्चैव पृष्ठतः कालयन्पशून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita walked ahead of them, great king, in high spirits, while Ekata and Dvita came behind, driving the animals."}},{"n":20,"text":"तयोश्चिन्ता समभवद्दृष्ट्वा पशुगणं महत् ।\nकथं न स्युरिमा गाव आवाभ्यां वै विना त्रितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great herd, the two began to worry: how could these cattle be ours without Trita?"}},{"n":21,"text":"तावन्योन्यं समाभाष्य एकतश्च द्वितश्च ह ।\nयदूचतुर्मिथः पापौ तन्निबोध जनेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two sinners spoke together, king of men; hear what the two, Ekata and Dvita, said to each other."}},{"n":22,"text":"त्रितो यज्ञेषु कुशलस्त्रितो वेदेषु निष्ठितः ।\nअन्यास्त्रितो बहुतरा गावः समुपलप्स्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita is skilled in sacrifices and firm in the Vedas; Trita will get many other cattle."}},{"n":23,"text":"तदावां सहितौ भूत्वा गाः प्रकाल्य व्रजावहे ।\nत्रितोऽपि गच्छतां काममावाभ्यां वै विनाकृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So let us two join together, drive off the cows and go; let Trita go where he likes, left without us."}},{"n":24,"text":"तेषामागच्छतां रात्रौ पथिस्थाने वृकोऽभवत् ।\nतथा कूपोऽविदूरेऽभूत्सरस्वत्यास्तटे महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they traveled by night, a wolf appeared on the road, and there was a great well not far off on the bank of the Sarasvati."}},{"n":25,"text":"अथ त्रितो वृकं दृष्ट्वा पथि तिष्ठन्तमग्रतः ।\nतद्भयादपसर्पन्वै तस्मिन्कूपे पपात ह ।\nअगाधे सुमहाघोरे सर्वभूतभयंकरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita, seeing the wolf standing ahead of him on the path, backed away in fear of it and fell into that well, deep, terrible and frightening to all creatures."}},{"n":26,"text":"त्रितस्ततो महाभागः कूपस्थो मुनिसत्तमः ।\nआर्तनादं ततश्चक्रे तौ तु शुश्रुवतुर्मुनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Trita, the fortunate best of sages, in the well, cried out in distress, and the two sages heard him."}},{"n":27,"text":"तं ज्ञात्वा पतितं कूपे भ्रातरावेकतद्वितौ ।\nवृकत्रासाच्च लोभाच्च समुत्सृज्य प्रजग्मतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Learning that he had fallen into the well, the brothers Ekata and Dvita, out of fear of the wolf and out of greed, abandoned him and went on."}},{"n":28,"text":"भ्रातृभ्यां पशुलुब्धाभ्यामुत्सृष्टः स महातपाः ।\nउदपाने महाराज निर्जले पांसुसंवृते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Left by his two brothers, greedy for the animals, that great ascetic lay in the waterless well, covered with dust."}},{"n":29,"text":"त्रित आत्मानमालक्ष्य कूपे वीरुत्तृणावृते ।\nनिमग्नं भरतश्रेष्ठ पापकृन्नरके यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita, finding himself sunk in the well, overgrown with creepers and grass, like a sinner in hell, best of Bharatas,"}},{"n":30,"text":"बुद्ध्या ह्यगणयत्प्राज्ञो मृत्योर्भीतो ह्यसोमपः ।\nसोमः कथं नु पातव्य इहस्थेन मया भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and afraid of death, being one who had not drunk soma, thought with his wise mind: how can I, staying here, drink soma?"}},{"n":31,"text":"स एवमनुसंचिन्त्य तस्मिन्कूपे महातपाः ।\nददर्श वीरुधं तत्र लम्बमानां यदृच्छया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking thus in that well, the great ascetic saw a creeper hanging there by chance."}},{"n":32,"text":"पांसुग्रस्ते ततः कूपे विचिन्त्य सलिलं मुनिः ।\nअग्नीन्संकल्पयामास होत्रे चात्मानमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the sage, imagining water in the dust-filled well, imagined the sacred fires and himself as the priest."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततस्तां वीरुधं सोमं संकल्प्य सुमहातपाः ।\nऋचो यजूंषि सामानि मनसा चिन्तयन्मुनिः ।\nग्रावाणः शर्कराः कृत्वा प्रचक्रेऽभिषवं नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having imagined that creeper as soma, the greatly austere sage, reciting the Rig, Yajur and Sama verses in his mind, made pebbles into pressing stones and carried out the pressing, king."}},{"n":34,"text":"आज्यं च सलिलं चक्रे भागांश्च त्रिदिवौकसाम् ।\nसोमस्याभिषवं कृत्वा चकार तुमुलं ध्वनिम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He made ghee of the water and set out the shares of the dwellers in heaven; having pressed the soma, he made a mighty sound."}},{"n":35,"text":"स चाविशद्दिवं राजन्स्वरः शैक्षस्त्रितस्य वै ।\nसमवाप च तं यज्ञं यथोक्तं ब्रह्मवादिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That sound, the voice of Trita as a student of the Veda, entered heaven, king, and he completed that sacrifice as the Veda-speakers prescribe."}},{"n":36,"text":"वर्तमाने तथा यज्ञे त्रितस्य सुमहात्मनः ।\nआविग्नं त्रिदिवं सर्वं कारणं च न बुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"While the great-souled Trita's sacrifice went on, all of heaven was shaken and did not understand the cause."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः सुतुमुलं शब्दं शुश्रावाथ बृहस्पतिः ।\nश्रुत्वा चैवाब्रवीद्देवान्सर्वान्देवपुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brihaspati heard that tumultuous sound, and the gods' priest, hearing it, spoke to all the gods."}},{"n":38,"text":"त्रितस्य वर्तते यज्ञस्तत्र गच्छामहे सुराः ।\nस हि क्रुद्धः सृजेदन्यान्देवानपि महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trita is performing a sacrifice; let us go there, gods. That great ascetic, if angered, might create other gods."}},{"n":39,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं तस्य सहिताः सर्वदेवताः ।\nप्रययुस्तत्र यत्रासौ त्रितयज्ञः प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, all the gods together went to where Trita's sacrifice was going on."}},{"n":40,"text":"ते तत्र गत्वा विबुधास्तं कूपं यत्र स त्रितः ।\nददृशुस्तं महात्मानं दीक्षितं यज्ञकर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there, the gods came to the well where Trita was, and saw that great soul consecrated in the rites of sacrifice."}},{"n":41,"text":"दृष्ट्वा चैनं महात्मानं श्रिया परमया युतम् ।\nऊचुश्चाथ महाभागं प्राप्ता भागार्थिनो वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, great-souled and full of supreme splendor, they said to the fortunate one: we have come seeking our shares."}},{"n":42,"text":"अथाब्रवीदृषिर्देवान्पश्यध्वं मां दिवौकसः ।\nअस्मिन्प्रतिभये कूपे निमग्नं नष्टचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sage then said to the gods: you dwellers in heaven, look at me, sunk in this fearful well, my senses lost."}},{"n":43,"text":"ततस्त्रितो महाराज भागांस्तेषां यथाविधि ।\nमन्त्रयुक्तान्समददात्ते च प्रीतास्तदाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, Trita gave them their shares in due form, joined with mantras, and they were pleased."}},{"n":44,"text":"ततो यथाविधि प्राप्तान्भागान्प्राप्य दिवौकसः ।\nप्रीतात्मानो ददुस्तस्मै वरान्यान्मनसेच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having received their shares as ordained, the gods, glad at heart, offered him whatever boon he wished."}},{"n":45,"text":"स तु वव्रे वरं देवांस्त्रातुमर्हथ मामितः ।\nयश्चेहोपस्पृशेत्कूपे स सोमपगतिं लभेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He chose this boon: you gods should rescue me from here, and whoever touches water in this well should gain the destination of soma-drinkers."}},{"n":46,"text":"तत्र चोर्मिमती राजन्नुत्पपात सरस्वती ।\nतयोत्क्षिप्तस्त्रितस्तस्थौ पूजयंस्त्रिदिवौकसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wave-filled Sarasvati rose up there, king, and lifted by her, Trita stood, honoring the dwellers in heaven."}},{"n":47,"text":"तथेति चोक्त्वा विबुधा जग्मू राजन्यथागतम् ।\nत्रितश्चाप्यगमत्प्रीतः स्वमेव निलयं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" the gods went back as they had come, king, and Trita too went happily to his own dwelling."}},{"n":48,"text":"क्रुद्धः स तु समासाद्य तावृषी भ्रातरौ तदा ।\nउवाच परुषं वाक्यं शशाप च महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angry, he then approached those two sage brothers and spoke harsh words and cursed them, that greatly austere one."}},{"n":49,"text":"पशुलुब्धौ युवां यस्मान्मामुत्सृज्य प्रधावितौ ।\nतस्माद्रूपेण तेषां वै दंष्ट्रिणामभितश्चरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Because you two, greedy for animals, ran off and left me, you shall roam about among fanged beasts in their very form."}},{"n":50,"text":"भवितारौ मया शप्तौ पापेनानेन कर्मणा ।\nप्रसवश्चैव युवयोर्गोलाङ्गूलर्क्षवानराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cursed by me for this sinful act, your offspring shall be wolves, tailed monkeys, bears and langurs."}},{"n":51,"text":"इत्युक्ते तु तदा तेन क्षणादेव विशां पते ।\nतथाभूतावदृश्येतां वचनात्सत्यवादिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had spoken thus, lord of the people, in an instant the two became so, by the word of the truthful one."}},{"n":52,"text":"तत्राप्यमितविक्रान्तः स्पृष्ट्वा तोयं हलायुधः ।\nदत्त्वा च विविधान्दायान्पूजयित्वा च वै द्विजान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too, Halayudha of boundless valor touched the water, gave various gifts and honored the Brahmins."}},{"n":53,"text":"उदपानं च तं दृष्ट्वा प्रशस्य च पुनः पुनः ।\nनदीगतमदीनात्मा प्राप्तो विनशनं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that well and praising it again and again, the steadfast Balarama then went on to Vinashana on the river."}}]}]}